  "content": {
    "id": "p10-q21-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "21",
    "prompt": "In a group of twenty students, there are seven who study chemistry, eight who study physics, and nine who study neither. If a student from this group is selected at random, find the probability that they study physics and chemistry.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\frac{1}{5}$",
      "worked": "Let $C$ and $P$ be the events that the selected student studies chemistry and physics respectively. Eleven students study at least one of these subjects.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Pr(C\\cup P)&=\\frac{20-9}{20}=\\frac{11}{20}\\\\\\Pr(C\\cap P)&=\\Pr(C)+\\Pr(P)-\\Pr(C\\cup P)\\\\\\Pr(C\\cap P)&=\\frac{7}{20}+\\frac{8}{20}-\\frac{11}{20}\\\\\\Pr(C\\cap P)&=\\frac{4}{20}\\\\\\Pr(C\\cap P)&=\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 42
  },
